def sort_list(head):
    if not head or not head.next:
        return head
    slow, fast, prev = head, head, None
    while fast and fast.next:
        prev, slow, fast = slow, slow.next, fast.next.next
    prev.next = None  # cut the list into two halves
    left = sort_list(head)
    right = sort_list(slow)
    return merge_two_sorted(left, right)
```

The `prev` pointer trails one step behind `slow` specifically so you can sever the link (`prev.next = None`) once you know where the midpoint is — without it you'd find the midpoint but have no way to cut the list there. Time is O(n log n), matching array merge sort; space is O(log n) for the recursion stack, not O(n), since no auxiliary array is built.

